---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Move a live database" hint="A 5 TB database keeps taking writes while you copy it. Choose how the copy stays in sync, how you check it, and how you cut over. A small seeded model of 1,000 rows (10 chunks of 100) runs the whole migration, and the same 200 writes arrive on the new database after the flip.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>The default is <b>dual-write</b>, <b>no verification</b>, a <b>big-bang</b> flip and the new id counter starting at the snapshot. It looks fine and is wrong: <b>151 rows diverged</b>, <b>42 new ids collide</b> with live rows, and a rollback <b>loses 200 writes</b>.</li>
    <li>Switch verification to <b>chunk checksums</b>: the differing chunks are found and re-copied, so the diverged rows fall to <b>0</b>. Row counts alone leave <b>116</b>, because a changed value does not change a count.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>snapshot + change log</b> with <b>reads first, then a short write freeze</b>: the lag of <b>20</b> entries is drained in a <b>2.25 second</b> freeze. With the big-bang flip the same 20 entries are dropped and <b>20 rows</b> diverge. <b>Stop-the-world</b> is exact but down for <b>6.9 hours</b>.</li>
    <li>Tick <b>leave a gap in the ids</b> to remove the collisions, and pick <b>freeze + reverse replication</b> to bring writes lost on rollback from <b>200</b> to <b>0</b>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg zdm" data-zdm>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Keep the copy in sync with <select class="pg-in" data-sync>
        <option value="stop">stop-the-world copy (writes off)</option>
        <option value="log">snapshot + change log</option>
        <option value="dual" selected>dual-write from the application</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Verify before cutover <select class="pg-in" data-verify>
        <option value="none" selected>nothing</option>
        <option value="counts">row counts</option>
        <option value="sums">chunk checksums</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Cutover <select class="pg-in" data-cut>
        <option value="big" selected>big bang, no freeze</option>
        <option value="freeze">reads first, then a short write freeze</option>
        <option value="reverse">freeze + reverse replication to the old database</option>
      </select></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-gap /> Leave a gap in the new id sequence</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Write downtime</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Rows that differ after cutover</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Writes lost on rollback</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Lag at cutover</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>New ids that collide</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 1,000 rows copied in 10 chunks while 50 writes arrive per tick (60% updates, 20% inserts, 20% deletes). Dual-write drops 3% of the writes to the new database, and the backfill copies the snapshot, so it can overwrite a newer value. The change log is applied 80 entries per tick until the lag is below 30. Copy time assumes 5 TB at 200 MB/s. A freeze costs 2 seconds to flip plus the lag at 80 entries per second. After the flip, 200 writes go to the new database.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-zdm]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    type Opt = { sync: string; verify: string; cut: string; gap: boolean };
    const MIX = { of: 10, updateBelow: 6, insertBelow: 8 }; // workload: 60% updates, 20% inserts, 20% deletes
    const VAL_RANGE = 1000; const ROWS = 1000; const CHUNK = 100; const CHUNKS = 10; // initial table and copy chunks
    const WRITES_PER_TICK = 50; const DUAL_DROP_PCT = 3; // dual writes to the new database fail 3% of the time
    const LOG = { catchUpLag: 30, applyPerTick: 80 }; // log replay stops chasing at 30 entries behind; applies 80 per second
    const ID_PROBE = 50; const ID_GAP = 1000; // new ids checked for collisions; gap left above the old maximum
    const NEW_WRITES = 200; // writes after the flip
    const PROD = { rows: 5e6, copyRowsPerS: 200 }; const SEC_PER_H = 3600; // full-size table and copy speed
    const FLIP_S = 2; const DOWNTIME_OK_S = 60;
      function simulate(o: Opt) {
    // Numerical Recipes LCG
    let seed = 7; const random = (n: number) => { seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296; return Math.floor(seed / 65536) % n; };
    class Db { rows: Map<number, number>; log: any[]; nextId: number; constructor() { this.rows = new Map<number, number>(); this.log = [] as any[]; this.nextId = 1; }
      set(id: number, v: number) { this.rows.set(id, v); this.log.push({ op: 'set', id, val: v }); }
      del(id: number) { this.rows.delete(id); this.log.push({ op: 'del', id }); }
      apply(e: any) { this.nextId = Math.max(this.nextId, e.id + 1); if (e.op === 'set') this.rows.set(e.id, e.val); else this.rows.delete(e.id); } }
    const workload = (db: Db, n: number) => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const r = random(MIX.of); if (r < MIX.updateBelow) db.set(1 + random(db.nextId - 1), random(VAL_RANGE)); else if (r < MIX.insertBelow) { const id = db.nextId++; db.set(id, random(VAL_RANGE)); } else db.del(1 + random(db.nextId - 1)); } };
    const bad = (a: Db, b: Db) => { const ids: number[] = []; for (let id = 1; id < Math.max(a.nextId, b.nextId); id++) if ((a.rows.get(id) ?? -1) !== (b.rows.get(id) ?? -1)) ids.push(id); return ids; };
    const src = new Db(); for (let i = 0; i < ROWS; i++) src.set(src.nextId++, random(VAL_RANGE)); src.log = [];
    const snap = new Map<number, number>(src.rows), snapNext = src.nextId, dst = new Db();
    const copy = (t: number) => { for (let id = 1 + t * CHUNK; id < 1 + CHUNK + t * CHUNK; id++) if (snap.has(id)) dst.rows.set(id, snap.get(id)!); };
    let applied = 0, lag = 0, ticks = 0;
    if (o.sync === 'stop') { for (let t = 0; t < CHUNKS; t++) copy(t); dst.nextId = src.nextId; }
    else if (o.sync === 'dual') { for (let t = 0; t < CHUNKS; t++) { copy(t); const from = src.log.length; workload(src, WRITES_PER_TICK); for (const e of src.log.slice(from)) if (random(100) >= DUAL_DROP_PCT) dst.apply(e); } dst.nextId = Math.max(dst.nextId, src.nextId); }
    else { for (let t = 0; t < CHUNKS; t++) { copy(t); workload(src, WRITES_PER_TICK); } while (src.log.length - applied >= LOG.catchUpLag) { workload(src, WRITES_PER_TICK); for (let k = 0; k < LOG.applyPerTick && applied < src.log.length; k++) dst.apply(src.log[applied++]); ticks++; } lag = src.log.length - applied; dst.nextId = Math.max(dst.nextId, src.nextId); }
    // verification, before the flip
    const chunkOf = (id: number) => Math.floor((id - 1) / CHUNK);
    const drain = o.cut !== 'big';
    if (o.sync === 'log' && drain) while (applied < src.log.length) dst.apply(src.log[applied++]);
    const found = { chunks: 0, count: 0 };
    let ids = bad(src, dst);
    found.chunks = new Set(ids.map(chunkOf)).size; found.count = Math.abs(src.rows.size - dst.rows.size);
    if (o.verify === 'counts') { for (const id of ids) if (src.rows.has(id) !== dst.rows.has(id)) { if (src.rows.has(id)) dst.rows.set(id, src.rows.get(id)!); else dst.rows.delete(id); } }
    else if (o.verify === 'sums') { for (const id of ids) { if (src.rows.has(id)) dst.rows.set(id, src.rows.get(id)!); else dst.rows.delete(id); } }
    dst.nextId = Math.max(dst.nextId, src.nextId);
    const diverged = bad(src, dst).length;
    let clash = 0; for (let k = 0; k < ID_PROBE; k++) if (src.rows.has(snapNext + k)) clash++;
    if (o.gap) clash = 0; else dst.nextId = snapNext;
    if (o.gap) dst.nextId = src.nextId + ID_GAP;
    dst.log = []; workload(dst, NEW_WRITES);
    const rev = o.cut === 'reverse';
    if (rev) for (const e of dst.log) src.apply(e);
    const lost = rev ? 0 : dst.log.length;
    const hours = PROD.rows / PROD.copyRowsPerS / SEC_PER_H;
    const freezeS = o.cut === 'big' ? 0 : FLIP_S + (o.sync === 'log' ? lag / LOG.applyPerTick : 0);
    return { diverged, lost, lag, clash, found, hours, freezeS, rollbackOff: bad(src, dst).length };
}

    const set = (i: number, v: string, n: string, c: string) => { q(`[data-o${i}]`).textContent = v; q(`[data-n${i}]`).textContent = n; q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${i}]`).style.setProperty('--c', c); };
    function draw() {
      const sync = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sync]').value; const verify = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-verify]').value; const cut = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cut]').value; const gap = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-gap]').checked;
      const r = simulate({ sync, verify, cut, gap });
      const stop = sync === 'stop';
      const downS = stop ? r.hours * SEC_PER_H + r.freezeS : r.freezeS;
      const downTxt = stop ? `${r.hours.toFixed(1)} hours` : `${r.freezeS.toFixed(r.freezeS % 1 ? 2 : 0)} seconds`;
      const probs: string[] = [];
      if (downS > DOWNTIME_OK_S) probs.push(`the service was read-only for ${r.hours.toFixed(1)} hours`);
      if (r.diverged > 0) probs.push(`${r.diverged} rows differ between the two databases`);
      if (r.clash > 0) probs.push(`${r.clash} of the first ${ID_PROBE} new ids hit live rows`);
      if (r.lost > 0) probs.push(`a rollback would lose ${r.lost} writes`);
      set(1, downTxt, stop ? 'every write waits for the whole copy' : cut === 'big' ? 'no freeze, so the writes still in the log are dropped' : `${FLIP_S} seconds to flip${sync === 'log' ? ` plus ${r.lag} entries drained at ${LOG.applyPerTick} per second` : ''}`, downS > DOWNTIME_OK_S ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      set(2, `${r.diverged} rows`, verify === 'none' ? `nobody looked; ${r.found.chunks} chunks were actually wrong` : verify === 'counts' ? `counts found ${r.found.count} missing or extra rows; changed values slip through` : `${r.found.chunks} wrong chunks found and re-copied`, r.diverged ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      set(3, `${r.lost} writes`, cut === 'reverse' ? 'the old database received every new write, so it is current' : `the old database never saw the ${NEW_WRITES} new writes`, r.lost ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      set(4, sync === 'log' ? `${r.lag} entries` : 'none', sync === 'log' ? (cut === 'big' ? 'flipped without draining: these writes are lost' : 'drained during the freeze, so nothing is lost') : 'there is no change log to be behind on', sync === 'log' && cut === 'big' ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      set(5, `${r.clash} of ${ID_PROBE}`, gap ? 'the new counter starts 1,000 above the old maximum' : 'the new counter restarts at the snapshot value, 1,001', r.clash ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', probs.length > 0);
      out.textContent = probs.length ? `Not safe to flip: ${probs.join('; ')}.` : `Clean migration: ${downTxt} of write downtime, 0 rows different, 0 writes lost if you roll back, and no id collisions.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
